 {
  "id": 645877,
  "url": "https://freesound.org/people/crosbychris/sounds/645877/",
  "name": "4th Aug 2022 - New Brighton beach on a Windy Day at Flood Tide.flac",
  "tags": [
   "Beach",
   "Estuary",
   "Flood",
   "H6",
   "Liverpool",
   "Mersey",
   "Ocean",
   "Sea",
   "Tide",
   "Water",
   "Waves",
   "Wind",
   "Windy",
   "XY"
  ],
  "description": "The sound of waves on a flat beach during flood tide on a windy day. \nRecorded at New Brighton beach in the Mersey Estuary on the Wirral peninsular. \nLong waves can be heard sweeping across flat sand towards my position with distant larger waves breaking on a sandbank further out. The tide is coming in, and by the end of the recording the water is a few inches deep around me. There was a strong breeze whipping up the waves in the estuary, but the zoom dead cat seems to do a good job of minimising the wind noise. \n\nRecording Date - 2022/08/04 - @12:50\n\nrecording equipment - Zoom H6 (40% gain)&gt;XYH6 mic (120°) + Zoom dead cat wind screen\n\n  Weather - sunny 16°C - North-Westerly wind (strong breeze)\n\nPost processing \nLow cut - 72 Hz (12 db)\nHigh Shelf - 1800 hz - 3 db\nNormalised to -3 dbfs\nFade in/out (3 secs)\n\nRecording format - Flack - 48000 hz - 24 bit",
  "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
  "type": "flac",
  "duration": 179.998,
  "samplerate": 48000.0,
  "username": "crosbychris",
